---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { val } from "../data/db.ts";
const build = val(`SELECT value FROM meta WHERE key='build'`);
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What wowforever.one collects, what it doesn't, and how to say no to analytics."
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Privacy" }]}
  {build}
>
  <header class="pt-8 pb-6 border-b border-rule">
    <h1 class="text-[2rem] leading-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[62ch] text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Short version: this site sets no cookies unless you allow analytics, and there is nothing else
      collecting anything about you.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="py-8 max-w-[72ch]">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-[1.35rem] mt-0 mb-2">Analytics</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mb-3">
      The site would like to count visits with <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong>, which sets cookies and
      sends a hashed identifier to Google. It is the only third-party script on the site.
    </p>
    <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mb-3">
      <strong>It does not load until you say yes.</strong> Every page ships with the analytics tag
      commented out in effect — a small script defines a loader function and nothing calls it. Choosing{" "}
      <em>No thanks</em> means that function is never invoked, this visit or any future one. Your answer is
      stored in your browser's <code class="font-mono text-[0.9em]">localStorage</code>, not on a server.
    </p>
    <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mb-3">
      If you allowed it and want to change your mind, clear site data for this domain — the question will
      come back. IP addresses are anonymised before they reach Google.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-[1.35rem] mt-8 mb-2">What the site doesn't do</h2>
    <ul class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed space-y-1.5 list-square ml-5">
      <li>No account, no sign-in, no email collection.</li>
      <li>No advertising networks, no ad slots, no pixel trackers.</li>
      <li>No server-side logs that identify you. This is a static site served from Cloudflare's edge.</li>
      <li>Nothing you read or click on this site is sold, shared, or reported anywhere.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-[1.35rem] mt-8 mb-2">Hosting</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Pages are served by Cloudflare. Cloudflare processes standard request data to deliver the site and
      defend it from abuse, under their own privacy terms — that is true of every website you visit, and it
      is not something this site can switch off.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-[1.35rem] mt-8 mb-2">Game data and artwork</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      The numbers on this site come from World of Warcraft's own client files. Artwork is reproduced from
      Blizzard's public press and marketing assets. No personal data is involved in any of it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-[1.35rem] mt-8 mb-2">Trademarks</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Unofficial fan resource. World of Warcraft, Warcraft and all associated assets are trademarks of
      Blizzard Entertainment, Inc. This site is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Blizzard.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
